nd expert ratings.", "Open seat: Dick Durbin (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Dick Durbin's retirement opened an open seat in a state that leans Democratic by about six points, and the 2026 environment adds further to the Democratic side. Lieutenant Governor Juliana Stratton enters as the clear favorite, having raised nearly $6 million and drawn heavy outside spending on both sides, while Republican Don Tracy has raised about $2.5 million and campaigned closely aligned with President Trump in a blue state.\n\nEvery major race rater calls the contest Solid or Safe Democratic, and prediction markets put Stratton's chances near 98 percent. No general-election polls are available, so the forecast rests on fundamentals and expert consensus, both of which point to a comfortable Democratic win of roughly fifteen points.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9877, "margin": 15.07}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9857, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9943, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9883, "margin": 15.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9819, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9928, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9849, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9898, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9888, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9865, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9862, "margin": 15.0}]}